      "side": 1,
      "message": "I missed this before but: why do we need a `WGPURequestAdapterWebGPUBackendOptions` on the `innerAdapterOption` at all? We just need it not to enumerate webgpu-on-webgpu backends, but it does that by default. And this also requires the inner implementation to support `WGPURequestAdapterWebGPUBackendOptions` but it shouldn\u0027t need to.\n\nCan this just be:\n\n```suggestion\n    // Pass through all of the core options. Note if backendType\u003dWebGPU,\n    // RequestAdapter will return null since it\u0027s not enabled by default.\n    WGPURequestAdapterOptions innerAdapterOption \u003d *ToAPI(*options);\n    // Don\u0027t pass through any of the extension options.\n    innerAdapterOption.nextInChain \u003d nullptr;\n```\n\nThen we can simplify other code, see comments above.",
